@loicmathieu Since Quarkus test classes are also beans, we need a way of knowing which test classes are indeed Quarkus tests.
You can follow the code starting from here: https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/master/test-framework/junit5/src/main/java/io/quarkus/test/junit/QuarkusTestExtension.java#L498

It should be pretty easy to provide a fix.
